    {
      "text": "Jesus: for he shall save his people from their sins, Matt. 1:21. Son of man came … to give his life a ransom for many, Matt. 20:28 (1 Tim. 2:6). blood … which is shed for many for the remission of sins, Matt. 26:28 (Luke 22:20). Lord God of Israel … redeemed his people, Luke 1:68. Lamb of God, which taketh away the sin of the world, John 1:29. through the redemption that is in Christ Jesus, Rom. 3:24 (Mosiah 16:15; 18:2; Morm. 9:12). we were reconciled to God by the death of his Son, Rom. 5:10 (Heb. 2:17). Christ died for our sins, 1 Cor. 15:3. Who gave himself for our sins, Gal. 1:4. we have redemption through his blood, Eph. 1:7 (Col. 1:14; Alma 5:27). he might redeem us from all iniquity, Titus 2:14. by his own blood … obtained eternal redemption for us, Heb. 9:12. Christ was once offered to bear the sins of many, Heb. 9:28. ye were not redeemed with corruptible things, 1 Pet. 1:18. Who his own self bare our sins in his own body, 1 Pet. 2:24. Christ also hath once suffered for sins, 1 Pet. 3:18. he is the propitiation for our sins, 1 Jn. 2:2 (4:10). he was manifested to take away our sins, 1 Jn. 3:5. washed us from our sins in his own blood, Rev. 1:5. thou wast slain, and hast redeemed us, Rev. 5:9.",
